The editor page
  In the page and beside it: KaTeX's style sheet and fonts (MIT; the fonts SIL Open Font
  License 1.1, as their name tables say), CodeMirror 5's style sheet (MIT), pdf.js and its
  worker (Apache-2.0), fflate (MIT), and in git.js isomorphic-git, lightning-fs, buffer and
  the small npm packages they depend on (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD, ISC, zlib); dist/LICENSES.txt
  lists each with its license text.
  Paper Modern, the page's text fonts: subsets of Andrey V. Panov's Computer Modern Unicode
  fonts (from the computer-modern npm package), renamed as the SIL Open Font License 1.1
  asks of a modified version; build/fonts/subset.py makes them, build/fonts/OFL.txt.
  IBM Plex Sans (400, 500, 600) and IBM Plex Mono (400, 500), the interface's fonts, in the
  page: Google Fonts' Latin cut as the @fontsource/ibm-plex-sans and @fontsource/ibm-plex-mono
  npm packages ship it, unchanged. Copyright 2017, 2019 IBM Corp., SIL Open Font License 1.1
  (these builds name no Reserved Font Name); dist/LICENSES.txt has the license as each package
  carries it, and the source is at github.com/IBM/plex.
  Loaded from jsDelivr while the page runs, not shipped: KaTeX with its mhchem extension,
